different, unbounded, globally-minimal hitting-set computation would be NP-hard. That establishes nothing against the target as stated.\n\nThe critic's argument depends entirely on replacing the target's bounded, canonical, fixpoint-reuse procedure with an unbounded global optimization and then attacking the replacement. No clause establishes that the target's actual procedure violates polynomial cost. The case fails."}